    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d795">

                <pb facs="0853" n="755" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg755"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.93/123</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Russian
                        Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ughet</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-04-10"><hi rendition="#italic">April 10,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of March 21, 1919, enclosing a memorandum relating to certain acts
                    of the Chinese Government affecting Russian interests, and to state that the
                    contents have been duly noted. I may add that, so far as the Chinese Eastern
                    Railway is concerned, this Government has consistently maintained that any
                    temporary operation of that road, as <pb facs="0854" n="756" xml:id="pg756"/> a
                    part of the trans-Siberian railway system, by the Inter-Allied Commission,
                    should be without prejudice to any previously existing rights, by whomsoever
                    held.</p>
                <p>A copy of your note under reply will be transmitted to the American Minister at
                    Peking.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Acting Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Alvey A. Adee</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
